<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48258" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thyestes</span></b> , ae,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θυέστης,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>son of Pelops and
				brother of Atreus</i>, <i>who set before him for
				food the flesh of his own son; he was the father of
				Ægisthus</i>, <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab.
				88</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plaut. Rud. 2, 6, 25</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Tusc.
				3, 12, 26</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. A. P. 91</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. C. 1,
				16, 17</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Pers. 5, 8</span></i>.— Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thyestēus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to Thyestes</i>, <i>Thyestean</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mycenae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					1, 544</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mensa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					P. 4, 6, 47</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. M. 15, 462</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exsecratio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Pis. 19, 43</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">preces,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					Epod. 5, 86</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">more furere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Contr. 1, 1 <i>med.</i></span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thyestĭădes</span></b> ,
			ae, m., <i>the</i> (male)
				<i>offspring of Thyestes;</i> said of <i>Ægisthus</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. A. A. 2,
				407</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Claud. VI. Cons. Hon.
			113</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
